    "body": "## Summary\n- persist private user-to-Stripe Connect recipient mappings with Flyway V44\n- add fail-closed, independently switchable Stripe-hosted Express onboarding\n- cache authoritative provider readiness without downgrading state on transient provider errors\n- expose onboarding status/link/refresh APIs and wallet UI flow, including Stripe refresh URL recovery\n- gate Stripe Connect payout reservation on connected-recipient readiness while leaving sandbox behavior unchanged\n- prevent unverified/inactive users from provisioning external Stripe accounts\n- document the operational kill switches and intentionally keep live money dispatch disabled until a separately reviewed provider adapter exists\n\n## Safety / accounting\n- no live `stripe-connect` PayoutProvider is registered in this PR; `PAYOUT_PROVIDER=stripe-connect` remains unavailable/fail-closed\n- wallet reservation and existing retry/review/restore semantics are unchanged\n- provider account IDs stay private and are not added to public/user payout history DTOs\n- onboarding redirect targets are fixed server config and HTTPS-only outside localhost\n\n## Verification\n- API unit coverage for recipient readiness gating and onboarding lifecycle\n- existing Maven verify, web audit/lint/build, PostgreSQL/container runtime smoke and payout smoke must pass before merge\n",
